{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":29204,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"e0bca2888db57115ace5792cbeb7211a74c22d7ef58b0d6eedc87ec6c6da41cf","packTokens":14378,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":143,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"sketches","tokens":14204,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":10,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"sketches"},"pointers":[],"system":"Three engineers independently listed behaviours for the same request. Find where they DISAGREE about what the system should do (not wording differences).\nFor each disagreement: id D-1.., the span, a short topic, and the readings: which sketch (1-3), which behaviour index (0-based) in that span, and a one-line summary. Cite at least two different sketches. Empty list if they agree.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"sketches\" kind=\"sketches\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"sketch\": 1,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-74-estimation-checklist\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Interpreted as a mandate for how estimation work itself must be produced: each listed area must be estimated independently rather than bundled into a single screen-count figure.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Given the checklist, the estimator produces a separate effort figure (e.g. hours/days) for each of the ~80 listed items across Product/UX, Frontend, Backend, Integrations, QA, DevOps and Documentation.\",\n     \"1: The final estimate output is a document/spreadsheet with one row per checklist item, not a single aggregate 'per screen' number.\",\n     \"2: Each checklist item estimate is recorded with at least: item name, category, estimated effort, and any assumptions used.\",\n     \"3: If an item cannot be estimated (e.g. because of an unresolved open question), the estimate row is flagged as 'blocked/assumption needed' rather than silently omitted or guessed as zero.\",\n     \"4: Only the implementation/estimation team produces and signs off the estimate; the client reviews but does not directly edit it.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-75-technology-stack\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Interpreted as a deliverable requirement: the implementation team must produce a formal technology proposal covering each listed concern, justified against stated non-functional requirements.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: The implementation team outputs a proposal naming a specific choice for each of: frontend framework, backend framework, database, authentication approach, file storage, email integration, PDF generation approach, hosting/cloud platform, CI/CD, monitoring/logging.\",\n     \"1: Each proposed technology choice includes a stated justification referencing expected scale and the 7-year data-retention requirement.\",\n     \"2: If a proposed technology cannot demonstrably support 7-year retention (e.g. no durable backup/archival story), that choice is rejected or flagged as needing a mitigation (e.g. archival export strategy).\",\n     \"3: The retention requirement is explicitly recorded as 7 years for order and invoice data when evaluating storage/database options.\",\n     \"4: The client approves/signs off the final stack choice before implementation proceeds; the implementation team cannot unilaterally lock it in without that approval.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-customer-auth-access\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers authentication and role-based access control as first-release features for a B2B portal with distinct customer, staff, and admin roles.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can register/log in with valid credentials and reach their company's authenticated area.\",\n     \"1: Staff and admin users log in via the same or a separate authenticated flow and are routed to role-appropriate dashboards.\",\n     \"2: Invalid credentials, expired sessions, or locked accounts produce a clear rejection rather than granting access.\",\n     \"3: Role-based access restricts which actions/screens a customer, staff member, or admin can perform (e.g. only admins can manage users; only staff/admin can create orders on behalf of customers).\",\n     \"4: User accounts are associated with a role and a customer/company record, persisted for use in access checks and data isolation.\",\n     \"5: A customer attempting to access another customer's data (orders, invoices, pricing) is denied — data isolation between customer accounts is enforced.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-catalogue-search\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers product catalogue, search/filtering, category filtering, and vehicle compatibility search as customer-facing discovery features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can browse the product catalogue and view product detail pages with current stock and price information.\",\n     \"1: A customer can search products by keyword, filter by category, and filter by vehicle compatibility (e.g. make/model/year) to narrow results.\",\n     \"2: Vehicle compatibility search returns only products marked compatible with the selected vehicle.\",\n     \"3: A search/filter with no matching products shows an explicit empty-state rather than an error or blank screen.\",\n     \"4: Product, category, and vehicle-compatibility data are stored and kept in sync with ERP stock import data.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-pricing-stock\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers customer-specific pricing and ERP stock import as backend/data-driven features affecting what customers see and can order.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each authenticated customer sees prices specific to their account/company (price list), not a single public price.\",\n     \"1: Stock levels are updated from periodic ERP CSV imports and reflected in product availability shown to customers.\",\n     \"2: An ERP import file that is malformed or missing required fields is rejected, with the failure logged and prior stock data left unchanged (no silent partial corruption).\",\n     \"3: A customer attempting to order more than available stock is blocked or warned at basket/checkout.\",\n     \"4: Each product carries current stock quantity and at least one price-list entry per eligible customer/company.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-basket-checkout\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers basket, checkout, delivery scheduling rules, and order placement as the core purchase flow.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can add/remove/update quantities of products in a basket that persists across sessions for that customer.\",\n     \"1: At checkout, the customer selects a delivery date/slot constrained by configured delivery scheduling rules (e.g. cut-off times, blackout days).\",\n     \"2: Submitting checkout with valid basket, address, and delivery choice creates a new order and clears/archives the basket.\",\n     \"3: Checkout is blocked if the basket is empty, an item has become out of stock, or a chosen delivery slot is no longer valid — with an explicit error shown to the customer.\",\n     \"4: A confirmed order records the ordered items, prices at time of order, chosen delivery date, and the customer/company it belongs to.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-orders-history-tracking\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers order history, order tracking, order cancellation, and repeat orders as post-purchase customer features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can view a list of their past orders and open an order-detail view showing items, status, and delivery info.\",\n     \"1: A customer can view current order status (tracking) that updates as the order progresses through defined states.\",\n     \"2: A customer can cancel an order while it is in a cancellable state, resulting in the order's status changing to cancelled.\",\n     \"3: A customer can re-order a past order ('repeat order'), pre-filling a new basket with the same items (adjusted for current stock/price).\",\n     \"4: Attempting to cancel an order that has already shipped/invoiced is rejected with an explanation.\",\n     \"5: A customer can only view/cancel/repeat their own company's orders, not another customer's.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-templates\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers saved basket templates allowing customers to store and reuse common order sets.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can save the current basket contents as a named template for future reuse.\",\n     \"1: A customer can load a saved template into the basket, overwriting or merging with current contents.\",\n     \"2: A customer can view, rename, and delete their saved templates.\",\n     \"3: Loading a template containing discontinued/out-of-stock items flags those items rather than silently adding them.\",\n     \"4: Templates are stored per customer/company, not shared across unrelated accounts.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-staff-order-management\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers staff order management and staff-created orders as internal-user features for handling customer orders on their behalf.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff can search/view all orders across customers and update order status (e.g. processing, shipped, cancelled).\",\n     \"1: Staff can create a new order on behalf of a specific customer, using that customer's pricing.\",\n     \"2: Attempting a disallowed status transition (e.g. shipped → pending) is rejected and logged.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin roles can access order-management tooling and create orders for other customers; regular customers cannot.\",\n     \"4: Staff-created orders and status changes are attributed to the acting staff user for audit purposes.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-delivery-csv-export\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers delivery CSV export as a staff/admin tool for fulfilling and scheduling deliveries.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff/admin can trigger a CSV export of orders scheduled for delivery, downloadable as a file.\",\n     \"1: Exported CSV contains relevant delivery fields (address, items, date/slot, order reference).\",\n     \"2: An export requested when there are no matching orders produces an empty/valid CSV with headers, not an error page.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin roles can generate delivery CSV exports.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-invoicing-payments\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers automated invoice creation, invoice PDFs, and payment status tracking as billing features tied to orders.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When an order reaches the relevant state (e.g. confirmed/shipped), an invoice is automatically generated and linked to that order.\",\n     \"1: A customer or staff member can view/download the invoice as a PDF.\",\n     \"2: Each invoice displays and stores a payment status (e.g. unpaid, paid, overdue) that can be updated.\",\n     \"3: Invoice PDF generation failure is retried/logged rather than leaving the order with no accessible invoice indefinitely.\",\n     \"4: Invoices and their PDFs are retained for at least 7 years per the retention requirement.\",\n     \"5: A customer can only view their own company's invoices.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-admin-management\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers product administration, price-list administration, and user administration as admin-only back-office features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: An admin can create/edit/deactivate products, categories, and vehicle-compatibility mappings.\",\n     \"1: An admin can create/edit customer-specific price lists and assign them to customers/companies.\",\n     \"2: An admin can create, edit, deactivate, and change the role of user accounts (customer, staff, admin).\",\n     \"3: Attempting to deactivate the last remaining admin account is rejected to prevent total lockout.\",\n     \"4: Only admin-role users can access product, price-list, and user administration screens; staff and customers cannot.\",\n     \"5: Administrative changes (product edits, price changes, user role changes) are written with the acting admin and timestamp.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-reporting-exports\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers reporting and CSV exports as admin/staff analytics features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff/admin can view reports (e.g. sales, order volume) filtered by date range/customer.\",\n     \"1: Staff/admin can export report data as CSV for offline use.\",\n     \"2: A report request for a date range with no data returns an empty result set with a clear message, not an error.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin can access reporting and CSV export features; customers cannot see cross-customer reports.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-notifications-audit\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers email notifications and audit history as cross-cutting system behaviours triggered by order/account events.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Email notifications are sent to customers on key events (e.g. order placed, order shipped, invoice generated).\",\n     \"1: An audit history log records significant actions (order status changes, admin edits, staff-created orders) with actor, timestamp, and action.\",\n     \"2: If an email fails to send, the failure is logged/retried and does not block the underlying action (e.g. order still gets created).\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin can view the audit history; customers do not see internal audit logs.\",\n     \"4: Audit log entries and relevant order/invoice records are retained for at least 7 years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"section-76-scope-responsive-retention\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers the responsive mobile-first buyer experience and the 7-year retention requirement as cross-cutting non-functional commitments.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer-facing screens (catalogue, basket, checkout, order history) render usably on mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports.\",\n     \"1: Order and invoice records remain queryable/accessible for at least 7 years after creation, even as volume grows.\",\n     \"2: Data approaching or exceeding the 7-year mark is archived rather than deleted, unless explicit deletion is separately requested/required.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 2,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"74-estimation-checklist\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This span is a process/deliverable requirement: the estimation must be produced as a set of separate line-item estimates (not a single screen-count-based number), covering every listed Product/UX, Frontend, Backend, Integrations, QA, DevOps, and Documentation item.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Produce an estimate document containing a distinct effort figure (e.g. hours/days) for every individual listed item (requirements clarification, UX flows, responsive layouts, etc.), not a single aggregate per-screen number.\",\n     \"1: Group estimate line-items under the stated categories: Product/UX, Frontend, Backend, Integrations, QA, DevOps, Documentation.\",\n     \"2: If an estimate omits any listed item (e.g. no separate figure for 'Audit logs' or 'CSV downloads'), the estimate is rejected/returned as incomplete.\",\n     \"3: If estimation is done purely by counting screens with no per-capability breakdown, flag as non-compliant with the checklist.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"75-technology-stack\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Interpreted as a deliverable requirement: the implementation team must produce an explicit, written technology proposal covering each listed concern, with justification against scale and 7-year retention needs.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Produce a written proposal naming a specific choice for each of: frontend framework, backend framework, database, authentication approach, file storage, email integration, PDF generation approach, hosting/cloud platform, CI/CD, monitoring/logging.\",\n     \"1: For each proposed technology, record justification that it supports expected scale and the 7-year data-retention requirement.\",\n     \"2: If a proposal is submitted missing a choice for one of the ten listed concerns, treat the proposal as incomplete and send it back.\",\n     \"3: If a chosen technology cannot demonstrably support 7-year retention (e.g. managed storage with shorter max retention, or no long-term archival option), reject that choice and require an alternative.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-auth\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Customer authentication and role-based access are core login/permission behaviours of the first release.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can log in with valid credentials and reach their authenticated account area.\",\n     \"1: A customer entering invalid credentials is shown an authentication error and not logged in.\",\n     \"2: Users are assigned roles (customer, staff, admin) and the UI/API restrict access to screens and actions according to role.\",\n     \"3: A customer attempting to access staff or admin-only screens/endpoints is denied access (e.g. 403).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-customer-company-management\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff/admin can create, view, edit and deactivate customer/company records.\",\n     \"1: Each customer account is associated with a company, and company-level settings (e.g. pricing tier) apply to all its users.\",\n     \"2: A customer can only see and manage data belonging to their own company, not other companies'.\",\n     \"3: Attempting to create a customer/company with missing required fields is rejected with a validation error.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-catalogue-search-filter-vehicle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Product catalogue, search, category filtering, and vehicle compatibility search are treated as distinct but related browsing behaviours.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Any authenticated customer can browse the product catalogue and view product listings with core details.\",\n     \"1: A customer can enter search terms and receive matching product results.\",\n     \"2: A customer can filter the catalogue/search results by category.\",\n     \"3: A customer can search by vehicle (e.g. make/model/year) and receive only products compatible with that vehicle.\",\n     \"4: Searches with no matching results return an empty-state result, not an error.\",\n     \"5: Invalid or malformed vehicle search input (e.g. unsupported make) returns a clear 'no match' message rather than a system error.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-pricing-stock\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Product prices displayed to a logged-in customer reflect that customer's (or their company's) specific price list/tier.\",\n     \"1: Stock levels imported from the ERP are reflected on product pages (in stock / out of stock / quantity available).\",\n     \"2: An automated ERP stock import job updates product stock data on a scheduled basis.\",\n     \"3: If the ERP import file is malformed or import fails, the system logs the failure and retains the last known good stock data rather than wiping it.\",\n     \"4: A customer attempting to order more than available stock is blocked or warned before order placement.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-basket-checkout-delivery\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can add/remove/update quantities of products in a basket that persists across sessions while logged in.\",\n     \"1: A customer can proceed through checkout, selecting delivery details and confirming the order.\",\n     \"2: Checkout applies delivery scheduling rules (e.g. cut-off times, available delivery dates) and shows only valid delivery slots to the customer.\",\n     \"3: A customer attempting to check out with an empty basket is prevented and shown a message.\",\n     \"4: A customer attempting to select a delivery date/time that violates scheduling rules (e.g. past cut-off) is blocked with an explanatory message.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-order-placement-history-tracking-cancel-repeat\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: On checkout completion, an order record is created and a confirmation is shown/sent to the customer.\",\n     \"1: A customer can view a list of their past orders (order history) and open an individual order's detail/tracking status.\",\n     \"2: A customer can cancel an order while it is in a cancellable state (e.g. before dispatch).\",\n     \"3: A customer can re-order a previous order ('repeat order'), repopulating the basket with the same items.\",\n     \"4: A customer attempting to cancel an order that has already shipped/invoiced is blocked with an explanatory message.\",\n     \"5: A repeat-order action where an original item is now out of stock or discontinued shows a warning and excludes/flags that item rather than failing the whole action.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-basket-templates\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer can save the current basket as a named template for later reuse.\",\n     \"1: A customer can load a saved template to repopulate the basket.\",\n     \"2: A customer can only see and use templates they (or their company) created, not other companies' templates.\",\n     \"3: Saving a template with a duplicate name (for that customer) is handled, e.g. with overwrite confirmation or forced unique naming.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-staff-order-mgmt-staff-created-orders-csv\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff users can view, search, and manage all customer orders (not just their own) from a staff dashboard.\",\n     \"1: Staff can create an order on behalf of a customer, selecting the customer/company and applying that customer's correct pricing.\",\n     \"2: Staff can export a delivery CSV file containing order/delivery data for a selected date range or order set.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin roles can access staff order management and CSV export; customers cannot.\",\n     \"4: CSV export with no matching orders produces an empty/valid CSV with headers rather than an error, or an explicit 'no data' message.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-invoicing-payment\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When an order reaches the defined trigger state, an invoice record is automatically created without manual staff action.\",\n     \"1: A customer or staff member can download/view the invoice as a PDF, correctly reflecting order line items, pricing, and company details.\",\n     \"2: Each order/invoice displays a payment status (e.g. unpaid, paid, overdue) that updates based on recorded payment events.\",\n     \"3: Attempting to generate an invoice PDF for a non-existent or deleted order returns an error, not a blank/corrupt PDF.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-admin-product-pricelist-user-mgmt\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Admin users can create, edit, and remove products, categories, and vehicle-compatibility mappings.\",\n     \"1: Admin users can create and edit price lists and assign them to customers/companies.\",\n     \"2: Admin users can create, edit, deactivate, and assign roles to user accounts.\",\n     \"3: Only admin role can access product administration, price-list administration, and user administration screens/endpoints.\",\n     \"4: Admin attempting to delete a product that is referenced by existing orders is blocked or the product is archived rather than hard-deleted.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-reporting-csv-notifications-audit\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Admin/staff can view reports (e.g. sales, order volume) within the admin area.\",\n     \"1: Admin/staff can export report data and other listed datasets as CSV files.\",\n     \"2: The system sends automated email notifications for key events (e.g. order confirmation, invoice issued, order status change).\",\n     \"3: An audit history log records who did what and when for key actions (order changes, admin edits, user changes), viewable by admin.\",\n     \"4: If an email notification fails to send, the failure is logged and does not block the triggering action (e.g. order placement still succeeds).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-scope-responsive-retention\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All customer-facing buyer screens (catalogue, basket, checkout, orders) render correctly and are fully usable on mobile, tablet, and desktop viewport sizes.\",\n     \"1: Order and invoice records (and their associated data needed to reconstruct them) are retained and remain accessible for at least seven years from creation.\",\n     \"2: Any scheduled data-cleanup or archival process must not delete order/invoice data before the 7-year retention period has elapsed.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-open-questions-dependency\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treated as a process gate: estimation/final scope cannot be finalized while open questions remain unresolved.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each unresolved item referenced in the Open Questions section is either answered by the client or explicitly recorded as a stated assumption before the final estimate is produced.\",\n     \"1: If the final estimate is produced without either a client answer or a documented assumption for an open question, treat the estimate as invalid/provisional.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 3,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"74-estimation-checklist\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treated as a process requirement: the estimate deliverable must break down effort by each listed item rather than by screen/page count.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Estimate document contains a separate effort line (hours/days) for each checklist item under Product/UX, Frontend, Backend, Integrations, QA, DevOps and Documentation.\",\n     \"1: Estimate is not expressed solely as a per-screen count; screen-count figures, if present, are supplementary to the itemised breakdown.\",\n     \"2: If an estimate omits any checklist item, it is rejected/flagged as incomplete before being sent to the client.\",\n     \"3: Each itemised estimate line can be reviewed, approved, or revised independently of the others.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"75-technology-stack\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The implementation team must produce and submit a written technology proposal covering each listed concern before build starts.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Proposal document lists a chosen option for each of: frontend framework, backend framework, database, authentication approach, file storage, email integration, PDF generation approach, hosting/cloud platform, CI/CD, monitoring/logging.\",\n     \"1: Each proposed technology choice is accompanied by a justification referencing expected scale and the 7-year data-retention requirement.\",\n     \"2: A proposal that omits a justification tying the database/storage choice to 7-year retention is flagged as incomplete and returned for revision.\",\n     \"3: Only the implementation team (not the client) is responsible for drafting the technology proposal; client approval is required before the stack is finalised.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-customer-auth-and-access\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers login/registration for customers plus role-based permission enforcement across the portal.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer enters valid credentials → is authenticated and redirected to their account/catalogue area.\",\n     \"1: Customer enters invalid credentials → sees an error message and is not logged in; account lockout/rate-limiting applies after repeated failures.\",\n     \"2: Users are assigned roles (e.g., customer, staff, admin) and each role sees only the features/screens/data permitted for that role.\",\n     \"3: A user attempting to access a page or action outside their role's permission is blocked and shown an access-denied response.\",\n     \"4: Login attempts and role assignments are recorded for later audit.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-customer-company-management\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff/admin can create and manage customer accounts and associated companies, including multi-user companies.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff/admin can create, edit, and deactivate a customer or company record, with changes saved and reflected immediately in listings.\",\n     \"1: Each customer record is linked to a company record enabling company-specific pricing and order history.\",\n     \"2: Attempting to save a company/customer record with missing required fields (e.g., name) is rejected with a validation error.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin roles can create or deactivate customer/company records; customers cannot edit other customers' data.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-catalogue-search-vehicle-compatibility\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Covers browsing the product catalogue, free-text search, category filtering, and searching by vehicle to find compatible parts.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer browses the product catalogue and sees paginated product listings with images, names, and prices.\",\n     \"1: Customer enters a search term → matching products are returned; applying a category filter narrows results further.\",\n     \"2: Customer selects a vehicle (make/model/year) → only parts compatible with that vehicle are shown.\",\n     \"3: Search with no matching results shows an explicit empty-state message rather than a blank page.\",\n     \"4: Vehicle compatibility search with no matches informs the customer no compatible parts were found.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-customer-specific-pricing\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Prices shown to a logged-in customer reflect their company's negotiated price list rather than a single public price.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Logged-in customer viewing a product sees the price associated with their company's assigned price list.\",\n     \"1: Price-list assignments are stored per company and applied consistently across catalogue, basket, and checkout.\",\n     \"2: If a product has no price entry for the customer's price list, the product is shown as unavailable/priced-on-request rather than showing an incorrect price.\",\n     \"3: Customers can only see their own company's prices; they cannot view or infer another company's pricing.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-erp-stock-import\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Stock levels are imported from the client's ERP system via scheduled/periodic CSV import rather than real-time API sync.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A valid ERP CSV file is imported and stock quantities/availability are updated for matching product SKUs.\",\n     \"1: An import file with malformed rows or unknown SKUs is rejected (or partially processed) and an error report is generated listing the failed rows.\",\n     \"2: Each import run is logged with timestamp, file name, number of records processed, and number of failures.\",\n     \"3: If stock for a product drops to zero, the product is marked out-of-stock and cannot be added to a basket.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"76-basket-checkout-delivery-scheduling\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Customers add items to a basket, proceed through checkout, and delivery date/slot options are constrained by configured scheduling rules.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer adds a product to the basket → basket quantity and total update immediately.\",\n     \"1: Customer attempts to add more units than are in stock → is blocked or quantity is capped with a warning message.\",\n     \"2: 